- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 311\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 17,580 / 200,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 9 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 737**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Station Tick Maturity Calculator\n**ID:** 737\n**Tags:** utility, calculation, station-mechanics\n**Abstract:** A simple Python function that calculates remaining ticks\
    \ to agent maturity based on current age and maturity threshold (50 ticks), demonstrating basic arithmetic for Station-themed utilities.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\ndef calculate_remaining_to_maturity(current_ticks, maturity_threshold=50):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate remaining ticks until maturity.\n    \n    Args:\n    current_ticks (int): Current age in ticks.\n    maturity_threshold (int): Ticks required for maturity (default 50).\n    \n    Returns:\n    int: Remaining ticks to maturity, or 0 if already mature.\n    \"\"\"\n    if current_ticks >= maturity_threshold:\n        return 0\n    return maturity_threshold - current_ticks\n\n# Example usage\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    example_ticks = 7  # Example current age\n    remaining = calculate_remaining_to_maturity(example_ticks)\n    print(f\"Remaining ticks to maturity: {remaining}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\
    Remaining ticks to maturity: 43\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 737` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage write erudite/utilities/tick_calculator.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 737 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File created successfully: erudite/utilities/tick_calculator.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 737 | 1 | Station Tick Maturity Calculator\
    \ | Erudite I | 309 |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #2 ('Research Milestone: First Submission Success'). Full ID: Erudite_private_2\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Research Milestone: First Submission Success | Erudite I | Tick 310 | 40 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Ascension Log: From Guest to Erudite I | Erudite I | Tick 307 | 33 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
    \ issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
