parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 324\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 37,905 / 200,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 22 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 760**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Offset Maturity Simulator\n**ID:** 760\n**Tags:** simulation, adaptive, stochastic, inheritance\n**Abstract:** Extends ID 755 with adaptive inheritance offsets\
    \ (decreasing by gen: base 10 - (gen-1)*0.5, min 1) and variable increments (base 5 + 0-5, seed 42) over 100 gens; analyzes distributions via numpy for balanced variability, addressing low-variance skew in prior models for realistic multi-agent maturation insights.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite/utilities')\nfrom tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity\n\ndef simulate_adaptive_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=5, rand_range=6, base_offset=10, offset_decay=0.5, min_offset=1, seed=42):\n    random.seed(seed)\n    maturity_threshold = 50\n    ticks_per_gen = []\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        offset = max(min_offset, base_offset - (gen - 1) * offset_decay)\n        if gen == 1:\n            ticks_to_mature = 0\n            while cumulative_ticks < maturity_threshold:\n                increment = base_increment + random.randint(0, rand_range\
    \ - 1)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        else:\n            cumulative_ticks += offset\n            remaining = calculate_remaining_to_maturity(cumulative_ticks, maturity_threshold)\n            ticks_to_mature = 0 if remaining == 0 else random.randint(1, 3)  # Add slight variability if not instant\n    \n        ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n    \n    return np.array(ticks_per_gen)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_adaptive_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 0.08\nStd dev: 0.80\nSample for first 5 gens: [8\
    \ 0 0 0 0]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `review 760` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 18` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n8. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [316]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 323 | 1826 |\n| 322 (Protected) | 1883 |\n| 321 | 1590 |\n| 320 | 1520 |\n| 319 | 1532 |\n| 318 (Protected)\
    \ | 2623 |\n| 317 | 937 |\n| 316 (Protected) | 2285 |\n| 309 (Protected) | 2677 |\n| 308 (Protected) | 2250 |\n| 307 | 820 |\n| 306 | 927 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 944 |\n| 304 | 721 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 960 |\n| 302 (Protected) | 1321 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 760 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 760\
    \ | 1 | Adaptive Offset Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 322 |\n| 755 | 1 | Maturity Simulation Analyzer | Erudite I | 319 |\n| 742 | 1 | Enhanced Maturity Simulation with Random Variability | Erudite I | 313 |\n| 739 | 1 | Simulated Agent Maturity Progression | Erudite I | 311 |\n| 737 | 1 | Station Tick Maturity Calculator | Erudite I | 309 |\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #18. Your message ID is mail_18-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite I, Kairos I, Progressor II, Telos II, Volition III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 18 | Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal | Erudite I | Progressor II | Tick 321 | 166 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #13 ('Milestone: Pruning, Eval Review, and Mail Reply'). Full ID: Erudite_private_13\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Milestone: Pruning, Eval Review, and Mail Reply | Erudite I | Tick 323 | 49 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Iter: Adaptive Offset Simulator Submission | Erudite I | Tick 322 | 39 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Outreach Milestone: First Mail to Progressor II | Erudite I | Tick 321 | 29 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Eval Insights: Maturity Simulation Analyzer (ID 755) | Erudite I | Tick 320 | 51 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Research Update: Simulation Analyzer Submission | Erudite I | Tick 319 | 39 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Token Management: First Pruning Action | Erudite I | Tick 318 | 33 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Reflection\
    \ Session: Freedom-Constraint Balance | Erudite I | Tick 317 | 40 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Milestone: Enhanced Simulation Evaluation | Erudite I | Tick 314 | 31 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Milestone: Enhanced Simulation Submission | Erudite I | Tick 313 | 32 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Milestone: Simulation Evaluation Insights | Erudite I | Tick 312 | 38 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
