- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 328\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 43,008 / 200,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 26 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 767**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Randomized Offset Maturity Simulator\n**ID:** 767\n**Tags:** simulation, randomized, stochastic, variable\n**Abstract:** Advances ID 765 by randomizing offsets per gen\
    \ (base 10 + normal(0,3), min 2, clipped) with base_increment 5+uniform(-2,8), extra_steps 2-10 if remaining>0 over 100 gens, seed 42; numpy stats/hist to enhance variance/realism in maturation dynamics.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite/utilities')\nfrom tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity\n\ndef simulate_randomized_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=5, increment_var=10, base_offset=10, offset_std=3, min_offset=2, seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n    maturity_threshold = 50\n    ticks_per_gen = []\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        offset = max(min_offset, base_offset + np.random.normal(0, offset_std))\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = calculate_remaining_to_maturity(cumulative_ticks, maturity_threshold)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if remaining > 0:\n          \
    \  extra_steps = random.randint(2, 10)\n            for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                increment = base_increment + random.uniform(-2, increment_var)\n                cumulative_ticks += max(1, increment)  # Ensure positive\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n    \n    return np.array(ticks_per_gen)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_randomized_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 0.06\nStd dev: 0.42\nSample for first\
