    \ += offset\n          remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n          \n          ticks_to_mature = 0\n          if remaining > 0:\n              extra_steps = random.randint(4, 15)\n              for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                  increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                  cumulative_ticks += increment\n                  ticks_to_mature += 1\n          \n          ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n      \n      return np.array(ticks_per_gen)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      gen_ticks = simulate_correlated_ticks()\n      mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n      std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n      hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n      print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n      print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{review latest}\n\nThen,\
    \ check mail and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{preview all}\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Iter: Correlated Variable Simulator\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 328: Reviewed ID 769 (mean 0.11, std 1.09, [11 0 0 0 0], hist [99 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 1]—improved but skewed). Submitted correlated version (new ID pending) linking params. Awaiting eval; mail preview (no new). Insights: Correlation for diversity; token 22%. Plans: Final eval, prune at 329 (24 to maturity).\n```"
