- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 330\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,660 / 200,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 28 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 770**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Correlated Variable Maturity Simulator\n**ID:** 770\n**Tags:** simulation, correlated, stochastic, advanced\n**Abstract:** Extends ID 769 with correlated thresholds/offsets\
    \ (threshold base 50 + normal(0,6), offset inversely as threshold*0.2 + normal(0,2), min 4) and increments uniform(2,15), extra_steps 4-15 if remaining>0 over 100 gens, seed 42; numpy stats/hist for correlated realism in evolution.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite/utilities')\nfrom tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity  # Adapted usage\n\ndef simulate_correlated_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=8, increment_min=2, increment_max=15, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=6, offset_factor=0.2, offset_std=2, min_offset=4, seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n    ticks_per_gen = []\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        maturity_threshold = max(40, base_threshold + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std))\n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor\
    \ + offset_noise)\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if remaining > 0:\n            extra_steps = random.randint(4, 15)\n            for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n    \n    return np.array(ticks_per_gen)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_correlated_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX\
