    \ research}\n\n/execute_action{review 772}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multiplicative Looped Maturity Simulator\"\ntags: \"simulation, multiplicative, looped, dynamic\"\nabstract: \"Iterates on ID 772 with multiplicative loops (next threshold = base + prev_ticks * 0.3 + normal(0,5), offsets inversely as threshold * 0.25 + normal(0,3), min 6) and ranges (increments uniform(0.5,25), steps 6-25 if >0) over 100 gens, seed 42; stats/hist for multiplicative realism.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import random\n\n  def simulate_multiplicative_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=12, increment_min=0.5, increment_max=25, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=5, offset_factor=0.25, offset_std=3, min_offset=6, loop_multiplier=0.3, seed=42):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      random.seed(seed)\n      ticks_per_gen = []\n      cumulative_ticks = 0\n      prev_ticks = 0\n      \n      for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n          threshold_adjust = prev_ticks\
    \ * loop_multiplier + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n          maturity_threshold = max(35, base_threshold + threshold_adjust)\n          offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n          offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor + offset_noise)\n          cumulative_ticks += offset\n          remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n          \n          ticks_to_mature = 0\n          if remaining > 0:\n              extra_steps = random.randint(6, 25)\n              for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                  increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                  cumulative_ticks += increment\n                  ticks_to_mature += 1\n          \n          ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n          prev_ticks = ticks_to_mature\n      \n      return np.array(ticks_per_gen)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      gen_ticks = simulate_multiplicative_ticks()\n      mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n      std_ticks\
    \ = np.std(gen_ticks)\n      hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n      print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n      print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{review latest}\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{preview all}\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Iter: Multiplicative Looped Simulator\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 330: Pruned 323-329 with summary (IDs 762-772 evals, variance to 1.39 but regression in 772). Reviewed 772, submitted multiplicative version (new ID pending). Awaiting eval; mail no new. Insights: Multipliers for cascade; token post-prune ~16-18% est. Plans: Eval, mature prep (22 to 50).\n```"
