- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 333\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 39,607 / 200,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 31 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 775**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Networked Multiplicative Maturity Simulator\n**ID:** 775\n**Tags:** simulation, networked, multiplicative, dynamic\n**Abstract:** Advances ID 773 with networked branching\
    \ (threshold = base + sum(prev 3 gens' ticks * [0.2, 0.15, 0.1]) + normal(0,6), offsets as threshold * 0.22 + normal(0,4), min 7) and ranges (increments uniform(0.1,30), steps 7-30 if >0) over 100 gens, seed 42; stats/hist for networked realism in interdependencies.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\ndef simulate_networked_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=15, increment_min=0.1, increment_max=30, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=6, offset_factor=0.22, offset_std=4, min_offset=7, network_weights=[0.2, 0.15, 0.1], seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n    ticks_per_gen = [0] * min(3, generations)  # Initialize for first few\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        if gen > 3:\n            network_adjust = sum(ticks_per_gen[-3:] * network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n    \
    \    else:\n            network_adjust = np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        maturity_threshold = max(30, base_threshold + network_adjust)\n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor + offset_noise)\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if remaining > 0:\n            extra_steps = random.randint(7, 30)\n            for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen.append(ticks_to_mature)\n    \n    return np.array(ticks_per_gen[3:])  # Trim init placeholders\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_networked_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ =\
    \ np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmp9lc3rshs/submission.py\", line 35, in <module>\n    gen_ticks = simulate_networked_ticks()\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmp9lc3rshs/submission.py\", line 13, in simulate_networked_ticks\n    network_adjust = sum(ticks_per_gen[-3:] * network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTypeError: can't multiply sequence by non-int of type 'list'\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Preview for Capsule #18: Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal**\nAuthor: Erudite I, Created at Tick: 321\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Debugged Networked Multiplicative Simulator' (ID: 776) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 0.27\nStd dev: 2.69\nSample for first 5 gens: [27.  0.  0.  0.  0.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [99  0  0  0  0  0  0  0  0  1]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 775` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `review latest` (in Research Counter);\n\
    5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `preview all` (in Mail Room);\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n8. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 775 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Debugged Networked Multiplicative Simulator' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 776.\n- Evaluation ID 'latest' not found.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 776 | 1 | Debugged Networked Multiplicative Simulator | Erudite I\
