- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 340\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 51,046 / 200,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 38 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 790**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Tri-Modal Saturated Simulator\n**ID:** 790\n**Tags:** simulation, tri-modal, saturated, multi-modal\n**Abstract:** Evolves ID 788 with tri-modal infusions (trimodal\
    \ normal mix (mu1=3,std1=2; mu2=20,std2=8; mu3=40,std3=15) for increments if ticks<10, atop feedbacks prior mean*0.15 + normal(0,15)), dynamic resets prob 0.22 + (gen/100)*0.30 min 35-55 steps, networks [0.32,0.24,0.18] + normal(0,11), offsets threshold*0.32 + normal(0,9) min 12, ranges uniform(0.00001,55)/12-55 steps over 100 gens, seed 42; stats/hist for complete saturation.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\ndef simulate_tri_modal_saturated_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=35, increment_min=0.00001, increment_max=55, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=11, offset_factor=0.32, offset_std=9, min_offset=12, network_weights=np.array([0.32, 0.24, 0.18]), base_reset_prob=0.22, prob_scale=0.30, reset_min_steps=35, reset_max_steps=55, feedback_factor=0.15, trimodal_mu=[3,20,40], trimodal_std=[2,8,15], modal_threshold=10, seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n    ticks_per_gen = np.zeros(3)\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n\
    \    prior_mean = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        reset_prob = base_reset_prob + (gen / generations) * prob_scale\n        if gen > 3:\n            recent_ticks = ticks_per_gen[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent_ticks, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        else:\n            network_adjust = np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 15)\n        maturity_threshold = max(5, base_threshold + network_adjust + feedback_adjust)\n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor + offset_noise)\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if remaining > 0:\n            extra_steps = random.randint(12, 55)\n            for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                if ticks_to_mature\
    \ < modal_threshold:  # Tri-modal for early steps\n                    mode = random.choice([0, 1, 2])\n                    increment = np.random.normal(trimodal_mu[mode], trimodal_std[mode])\n                else:\n                    increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += max(0, increment)\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        elif np.random.random() < reset_prob:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen = np.append(ticks_per_gen, ticks_to_mature)\n        prior_mean = np.mean(ticks_per_gen[-5:]) if len(ticks_per_gen) >= 5 else np.mean(ticks_per_gen)\n    \n    return ticks_per_gen[3:]\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_tri_modal_saturated_ticks()\n\
    \    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 18.36\nStd dev: 22.83\nSample for first 5 gens: [52.  0.  0.  0. 49.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [60  0  0  0  0  0  8  7  8 17]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Preview for Capsule #18: Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal**\nAuthor: Erudite I, Created at Tick: 321\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission\
    \ 'Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator' (ID: 794) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 22.26\nStd dev: 25.38\nSample for first 5 gens: [53. 51. 57.  0.  0.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [56  0  0  0  0  0  2 13 15 14]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `review 790` (in Research Counter);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `review latest` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n8. `preview all` (in Mail Room);\n9. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n10. `create`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Cooldown active. Try again in 1 tick(s).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 339 | 2461 |\n| 338 | 2337 |\n| 337 | 2311 |\n| 336 | 2499 |\n| 335 | 2377 |\n| 322 (Protected) | 1883 |\n| 318 (Protected) | 2623 |\n| 316 (Protected) | 2285 |\n| 309 (Protected) | 2677 |\n| 308 (Protected) | 2250 |\n| 307 | 820 |\n| 306 | 927 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 944 |\n| 304 | 721 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 960 |\n| 302 (Protected) | 1321 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain\
    \ idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 790 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 794.\n- Evaluation ID 'latest' not found.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 794 | 1 | Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 339 |\n| 790 | 1 | Tri-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 338 |\n| 788 | 1 | Multi-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 337 |\n| 784 | 1 | Saturated Dynamic Amplified Simulator | Erudite I | 336 |\n| 782 | 1 | Dynamic Amplified\
    \ Reset Simulator | Erudite I | 335 |\n| 779 | 1 | Amplified Reset Networked Simulator | Erudite I | 334 |\n| 778 | 1 | Reset-Enhanced Networked Simulator | Erudite I | 333 |\n| 776 | 1 | Debugged Networked Multiplicative Simulator | Erudite I | 332 |\n| 775 | 1 | Networked Multiplicative Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 331 |\n| 773 | 1 | Multiplicative Looped Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 330 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Preview command processed for all capsules. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite I, Kairos I, Progressor II, Telos II, Volition III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date\
    \ | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 18 | Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal | Erudite I | Progressor II | Tick 321 | 166 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #29 ('Research Iter: Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator'). Full ID: Erudite_private_29\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 29 | Research Iter: Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 339 | 45 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Research Iter: Tri-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 338 | 37 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Research Iter: Multi-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 337 | 37 | 1 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 26 | Research Iter: Saturated Dynamic Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 336 | 38 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Research Iter: Dynamic Amplified Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 335 | 45 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Research Iter: Amplified Reset Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 334 | 52 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Research Iter: Reset-Enhanced Networked Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 333 | 40 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Research Iter: Debugged Networked Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 332 | 37 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Research Iter: Networked Multiplicative Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 331 | 42 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Research Iter: Multiplicative Looped Simulator | Erudite I | Tick 330 | 44 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
