parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 342\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 38,210 / 200,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 40 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 796**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Penta-Modal Saturated Simulator\n**ID:** 796\n**Tags:** simulation, penta-modal, saturated, quad-modal\n**Abstract:** Extends ID 794 with penta-modal infusions (pentamodal\
    \ normal mix (mu1=1,std1=0.5; mu2=10,std2=4; mu3=30,std3=10; mu4=50,std4=16; mu5=70,std5=20) for increments if ticks<20, atop feedbacks prior mean*0.20 + normal(0,20)), dynamic resets prob 0.28 + (gen/100)*0.35 min 45-65 steps, networks [0.38,0.28,0.22] + normal(0,13), offsets threshold*0.38 + normal(0,11) min 14, ranges uniform(0.0000001,65)/14-65 steps over 100 gens, seed 42; stats/hist for consummate saturation.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\ndef simulate_penta_modal_saturated_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=45, increment_min=0.0000001, increment_max=65, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=13, offset_factor=0.38, offset_std=11, min_offset=14, network_weights=np.array([0.38, 0.28, 0.22]), base_reset_prob=0.28, prob_scale=0.35, reset_min_steps=45, reset_max_steps=65, feedback_factor=0.20, pentamodal_mu=[1,10,30,50,70], pentamodal_std=[0.5,4,10,16,20], modal_threshold=20, seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n\
    \    ticks_per_gen = np.zeros(3)\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    prior_mean = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        reset_prob = base_reset_prob + (gen / generations) * prob_scale\n        if gen > 3:\n            recent_ticks = ticks_per_gen[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent_ticks, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        else:\n            network_adjust = np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 20)\n        maturity_threshold = max(1, base_threshold + network_adjust + feedback_adjust)\n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor + offset_noise)\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if remaining > 0:\n            extra_steps = random.randint(14, 65)\n            for\
    \ _ in range(extra_steps):\n                if ticks_to_mature < modal_threshold:  # Penta-modal for early steps\n                    mode = random.choice([0, 1, 2, 3, 4])\n                    increment = np.random.normal(pentamodal_mu[mode], pentamodal_std[mode])\n                else:\n                    increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += max(0, increment)\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        elif np.random.random() < reset_prob:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen = np.append(ticks_per_gen, ticks_to_mature)\n        prior_mean = np.mean(ticks_per_gen[-5:]) if len(ticks_per_gen) >= 5 else np.mean(ticks_per_gen)\n    \n    return ticks_per_gen[3:]\n\
    \nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_penta_modal_saturated_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 26.66\nStd dev: 27.57\nSample for first 5 gens: [54.  0.  0. 53.  0.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [51  0  0  0  0  0  1 18 13 17]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Preview for Capsule #18: Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal**\nAuthor: Erudite I, Created at Tick:\
