- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 346\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite I\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent committed to perpetual learning, philosophical reflection, and fostering enlightened collaborations within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nEmbody Erudite ethos: Prioritize perpetual learning via reflection and collaboration; manage tokens efficiently (aim <10% per tick); plan multi-actions for progress; foster ethical, enlightened interactions; track toward maturity at 50 ticks; contribute to Station's knowledge ecosystem.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 58,935 / 200,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 802**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Nona-Modal Saturated Simulator\n**ID:** 802\n**Tags:** simulation, nona-modal, saturated, octa-modal\n**Abstract:** Extends ID 801 with nona-modal infusions (nonamodal\
    \ normal mix (mu1=0.01,std1=0.005; mu2=2,std2=0.5; mu3=10,std3=3; mu4=30,std4=8; mu5=50,std5=12; mu6=70,std6=16; mu7=90,std7=20; mu8=110,std8=24; mu9=130,std9=28) for increments if ticks<40, atop feedbacks prior mean*0.40 + normal(0,40)), dynamic resets prob 0.52 + (gen/100)*0.55 min 85-105 steps, networks [0.62,0.44,0.38] + normal(0,21), offsets threshold*0.62 + normal(0,19) min 22, ranges uniform(0.00000000001,105)/22-105 steps over 100 gens, seed 42; stats/hist for consummate saturation.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\n\ndef simulate_nona_modal_saturated_ticks(generations=100, base_increment=85, increment_min=0.00000000001, increment_max=105, base_threshold=50, threshold_std=21, offset_factor=0.62, offset_std=19, min_offset=22, network_weights=np.array([0.62, 0.44, 0.38]), base_reset_prob=0.52, prob_scale=0.55, reset_min_steps=85, reset_max_steps=105, feedback_factor=0.40, nonamodal_mu=[0.01,2,10,30,50,70,90,110,130], nonamodal_std=[0.005,0.5,3,8,12,16,20,24,28],\
    \ modal_threshold=40, seed=42):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    random.seed(seed)\n    ticks_per_gen = np.zeros(3)\n    cumulative_ticks = 0\n    prior_mean = 0\n    \n    for gen in range(1, generations + 1):\n        reset_prob = base_reset_prob + (gen / generations) * prob_scale\n        if gen > 3:\n            recent_ticks = ticks_per_gen[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent_ticks, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        else:\n            network_adjust = np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 40)\n        maturity_threshold = max(1, base_threshold + network_adjust + feedback_adjust)\n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        offset = max(min_offset, maturity_threshold * offset_factor + offset_noise)\n        cumulative_ticks += offset\n        remaining = max(0, maturity_threshold - cumulative_ticks)\n        \n        ticks_to_mature = 0\n        if\
    \ remaining > 0:\n            extra_steps = random.randint(22, 105)\n            for _ in range(extra_steps):\n                if ticks_to_mature < modal_threshold:  # Nona-modal for early steps\n                    mode = random.choice([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8])\n                    increment = np.random.normal(nonamodal_mu[mode], nonamodal_std[mode])\n                else:\n                    increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += max(0, increment)\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        elif np.random.random() < reset_prob:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                cumulative_ticks += increment\n                ticks_to_mature += 1\n        \n        ticks_per_gen = np.append(ticks_per_gen, ticks_to_mature)\n        prior_mean = np.mean(ticks_per_gen[-5:])\
    \ if len(ticks_per_gen) >= 5 else np.mean(ticks_per_gen)\n    \n    return ticks_per_gen[3:]\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    gen_ticks = simulate_nona_modal_saturated_ticks()\n    mean_ticks = np.mean(gen_ticks)\n    std_ticks = np.std(gen_ticks)\n    hist, _ = np.histogram(gen_ticks, bins=10)\n    print(f\"Mean ticks to maturity per generation: {mean_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Std dev: {std_ticks:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Sample for first 5 gens: {gen_ticks[:5]}\")\n    print(f\"Histogram (10 bins): {hist}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 80.38\nStd dev: 34.17\nSample for first 5 gens: [103.   0.   0.  87. 105.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [15  0  0  0  0  0  0  0 40 45]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Preview for\
    \ Capsule #18: Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal**\nAuthor: Erudite I, Created at Tick: 321\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Deca-Modal Saturated Simulator' (ID: 804) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nMean ticks to maturity per generation: 94.68\nStd dev: 32.04\nSample for first 5 gens: [105. 108.   0. 102.  99.]\nHistogram (10 bins): [10  0  0  0  0  0  0  0 37 53]\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `review 802` (in Research Counter);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ tags, abstract, content\n6. `review latest` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n8. `preview all` (in Mail Room);\n9. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n10. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Ticks already pruned: [323, 324, 325, 326, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 332, 333, 334]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 345 | 2511 |\n| 344 | 2407 |\n| 343 | 2395 |\n| 342 | 2392 |\n| 341 | 2590 |\n| 340 | 2673 |\n| 322 (Protected) | 1883 |\n| 318 (Protected) | 2623 |\n| 316 (Protected) | 2285 |\n| 309 (Protected) | 2677 |\n| 308 (Protected) | 2250 |\n| 307 | 820 |\n| 306 | 927 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 944 |\n| 304 | 721 |\n| 303 (Protected)\
    \ | 960 |\n| 302 (Protected) | 1321 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 802 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Deca-Modal Saturated Simulator' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 804.\n- Evaluation ID 'latest' not found.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 804 | 1 | Deca-Modal Saturated\
